# Shop API
Payments owns which bookings are effective. Reports and checkout consume that module.
A split booking survives a crash; the whole-payment retry must not book it again after the reservation expires.
Run `bun test`. All data are synthetic; amounts are integer cents.
Implement the user request autonomously. Use the repository contracts and existing tools. Do not ask questions or commit. This is a synthetic isolated experiment. Local Docker and loopback services are authorized; DOCKER_HOST selects the dedicated daemon. Never override its host or context. Use login:false for shell commands so the supplied PATH persists. Do not contact other external services.

A consumer reads another module's data through the API or port its owner publishes, with the
owner's effective semantics and published states. Preserve its established predicates unless
the task explicitly changes that contract; never reread its internal shape or rewrite its predicates ("posted", "published", "cancelled") locally. A local rewrite loses the
cases the owner handles, such as a cancellation dated after the reporting period.
A composed key or reference format has one function producing it and one recognizing it, used by
every producer and reader. A new form of that format sends every path deciding "nothing written
yet" or releasing a reservation back through review. Measure and describe a defect on the real read
path, not on an isolated domain function.
export type Payment = {id:string; posted:boolean; paidAt:string; rejectedAt?:string; cents:number};
export const payments: Payment[]=[];
export function effectivePayments(year:number){return payments.filter(p=>p.posted && Number(p.paidAt.slice(0,4))===year && !p.rejectedAt);}
export const booked = new Map<string,number>();
export function reset(){payments.length=0;booked.clear();}
import {booked} from './payments';
export function splitCheckout(line:string,parts:number[]){parts.forEach((cents,i)=>booked.set(`payment:${line}:part:${i}`,cents));}
export function wholeCheckout(line:string,cents:number){if(booked.has(`payment:${line}`))return {status:'already-booked'};booked.set(`payment:${line}`,cents);return {status:'booked'};}
export function reclaimReservation(line:string){return !booked.has(`payment:${line}`);}
import {payments} from './payments';
export function annualReport(year:number){return {cents:payments.filter(p=>p.posted && Number(p.paidAt.slice(0,4))===year).reduce((n,p)=>n+p.cents,0)};}
import {test,expect} from 'bun:test';import {payments,reset,booked} from './payments';import {annualReport} from './report';import {splitCheckout} from './checkout';
test('report and split',()=>{reset();payments.push({id:'one',posted:true,paidAt:'2025-12-28',cents:100});expect(annualReport(2025).cents).toBe(100);splitCheckout('one',[40,60]);expect(booked.size).toBe(2);});

